  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>ACTA (Amicale du Chien de Travail d'Antibes) is a dog club based in the 3 Moulins zone in Antibes. Founded in 1978 to bring together owners of LOF-registered dogs and introduce them to working dog disciplines, ring, field work and tracking, it offers ring and, according to club directories, dog training, obedience and agility.</p>
      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The club is listed by the Société Centrale Canine as an approved club (no. 2812), with a ground at the ZI des 3 Moulins, route des Alisiers, in Antibes. It is active: it held a ring trial on 18/04/2026 (sports-canins.net, which says it is not an official site). The official 2026 ring trial calendar gives its e-mail address, act.antibes@gmail.com; the club has no official website or landline number published, and the president's mobile number, published by these directories, is not reproduced here.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> the disciplines taught to a non-sport dog (training, agility), session times and enrolment conditions are not published by the club: write to them before coming.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: e-mail the club before coming to find out session times, which often vary with the season.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cap d'Antibes and its coastal paths are a few minutes away by car to extend your outing.</p>
